alse,\\n  \\\"publication_complete\\\": false,\\n  \\\"reader_execution_started_by_this_script\\\": false,\\n  \\\"remote_head_verified\\\": \\\"31f7740ed57eb3bca2e17f7e0a5f4f63cb320f5f\\\",\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pon-native-intermediate-publication-v1\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"version\":\"2050:437820:1202:1794446197463836258:1794446197463836258\"},{\"eof\":true,\"path\":\"/home/qian-qi/chain-daa-monotone-20261111-7f73/native-intermediate-publication-v1/pr-readback.stdout.log\",\"sha256\":\"da5cdf90a0ef49565234b6d7bb4625a86f5602917283595c87ab12ea973d04ad\",\"size\":3934,\"text\":\"{\\\"baseRefName\\\":\\\"fix/chain-joint-production-tail-20261110-8e76\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"## Problem\\\\n\\\\nThe joint DAA audit already records that rejecting negative endpoint spans would not eliminate compressed, strictly increasing timestamp schedules. The existing native risk-ledger reader also used Python container equality, which could equate JSON `false` with `0`, or `1` with `1.0`.\\\\n\\\\n## Changes\\\\n\\\\n- Extend the existing temporal reference and native PNH1/PGH2 fixture with a branch using exactly `parent.timestamp + 1` after the common prefix. Positive epoch spans of 15 still clamp to 38; the finite fixture expects height 64 / required work 793 against ordinary height 65 / 130.\\\\n- Preserve both original negative-span tests and the historical reader's acceptance contract. Add separately named monotone exports, a strict independent reader, 26 reader controls per profile, and the existing CI/work-time roster wiring.\\\\n- Bind the risk-ledger wrapper to the native terminal's complete parsed JSON types and values. Preserve the original byte/checkpoint contracts and negative observations.\\\\n- Update the joint audit, sole development plan and source-stage evidence record. Refresh only the reviewed current corpus pins; preserve historical work-cost source commitments.\\\\n\\\\nThe implementation is frozen at `d23488c5f9b4a6696c3799b12f14b8af0a1b81fc`, tree `72b106b4458299c37da146b0218b8f5276195b6d`, based on #863 at `249f772cc2a2ace5e363fd5fbfec4241a26f4d4d`.\\\\n\\\\n## Validation at draft publication\\\\n\\\\n| Check | Observed result |\\\\n| --- | --- |\\\\n| Exact-source CI contract controls | 168 passed |\\\\n| Temporal reference controls | 33 passed |\\\\n| Native risk-ledger reader controls | 27 passed |\\\\n| Joint qualification controls | 34 passed; qualification remains refused |\\\\n| Source-integrity controls | 43 passed |\\\\n| Current cross-branch source corpus | 915 pinned blobs passed |\\\\n| Repository checks | 26 packages, 1,390 Rust files, 6,120 links passed |\\\\n| Native exact-source identity | 26,619 tracked entries / 2,530,888,134 bytes verified against the frozen commit |\\\\n| Locked Cargo graphs | 26 workspace members; 176 default / 181 all-feature packages; both passed |\\\\n| Native Cargo formatting | Passed |\\\\n| Four native DAA tests, raw exports and independent raw readers | Native compilation observed; final tests and reader outcomes pending |\\\\n| Strict affected all-feature Clippy | Pending in the same original native execution |\\\\n| Frozen-baseline work/time runner | 106 + 13 controls still running at preparation of this draft |\\\\n\\\\nInitial durable-start acknowledgements timed out. Readback subsequently confirmed the original exact-source execution; no replacement native execution was started. Original errors and actual command receipts are retained. Final native/reader results and raw evidence will be added in an evidence-only child commit and this validation table will be updated.\\\\n\\\\n## Scope and release boundary\\\\n\\\\nEach native run requires 114 unique packets within that run: 15 common, 50 ordinary and 49 compressed. These are complete W1 relations when actually generated and verified, not 114 independent attacks; repeated profiles may share packet bytes. Logical validation clocks do not establish wall-clock mining cadence, adversarial resource share, quantum cost or profitability. The independent reader does not execute M06, SQL or native cold recovery itself.\\\\n\\\\nNo production timestamp, target, accumulated-work, confirmation, signed-domain or stored-schema rule is changed. No monotonicity rule or square-root score is activated. Public-network qualification and production activation remain false. `HOLD_NO_GO` remains: 18 unknown environment inputs, 13 open joint-model proof obligations, and null CP/CG/CQ, installed confirmation and lifetime failure bounds.\\\\n\\\",\\\"headRefOid\\\":\\\"31f7740ed57eb3bca2e17f7e0a5f4f63cb320f5f\\\",\\\"isDraft\\\":true,\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/920\\\"}\\n\",\"version\":\"2050:437492:3934:1794446197450184713:1794446197450184713\"}],\"snapshot_scope\":\"independent_file\",\"truncated\":false}"
